{
 "what": "The blank-line check (a found line with fewer than 50 edges per 10,000 pixels is not recognized; an edge: the grey level changes by at least max(24, contrast / 4) within 2 pixels, across or down) on vita-vn-ocr's linefind development regions, read by the overlay's own adapter (vjo-ocr --lines, the line finder and the pinned recognizer as the game worker runs them), as captured (x1) and in seven softer display paths of the same screenshots. A found line is 'text' when it overlaps a hand-marked line box (at least 10% of either box), 'empty' when it overlaps none, 'ignored' when it overlaps only a box marked ignore. 'rules' recounts every line in numpy under the rule PR #84 first had (1-pixel steps of contrast / 2: audit-overlay-dialogue-1 B2) and the current one ('current' equals the C's count on every line). Counts, rates and times only; no pixels or text.",
 "how": "python3 tools/blank_lines_eval.py --ocr build/host/vjo-ocr --models DIR --vocr-repo VITA_VN_OCR --shots DIR... --rules --out x1.jsonl; the same with --model VOCR3_FL10_w8.vocr --how x2-nearest --how x2-bilinear --how x2-bil-box1 --how sub720-bilin --how sub640-bilin --how blur1.0 --how blur1.5; python3 tools/blank_lines_eval.py --summary (both)",
 "display_paths": {
  "x1": "the screenshot as captured",
  "x2-nearest": "PSP rows: the 480x272 frame shown 2x without filtering",
